==================================================================================================
V4 DIRECT READOUT — does the circuit-count win survive without QPE?
==================================================================================================
  R=0.6, 4096 shots/circuit, 5 repeats. QPE numbers are k=4, the shipping default.

  ===== H2 | M=8 | G=2 | qubits 2 =====
  method               circuits   depth  total cx      cos   x PS cx
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift            32      10        32   1.0000      1.00
  QLTO V3 (QPE k=4)           4     614      1292   0.9777     40.38
  QLTO V4 (direct)            8      17        40   0.9939      1.25
    V4 norm ratio |g|/|gx| = 0.8644   (sinc(R) = 0.9411 is the predicted attenuation)

  ===== MaxCut N=4 | M=16 | G=1 | qubits 4 =====
  method               circuits   depth  total cx      cos   x PS cx
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift            32      12        96   1.0000      1.00
  QLTO V3 (QPE k=4)           4     223       636   0.9678      6.62
  QLTO V4 (direct)            4      19        44   0.9743      0.46
    V4 norm ratio |g|/|gx| = 0.8810   (sinc(R) = 0.9411 is the predicted attenuation)

  ===== Heisenberg N=4 | M=16 | G=3 | qubits 4 =====
  method               circuits   depth  total cx      cos   x PS cx
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift            96      12       288   1.0000      1.00
  QLTO V3 (QPE k=4)           4    1160      2236   0.9833      7.76
  QLTO V4 (direct)           12      19       132   0.9906      0.46
    V4 norm ratio |g|/|gx| = 0.8148   (sinc(R) = 0.9411 is the predicted attenuation)

  ===== Heisenberg N=6 | M=24 | G=3 | qubits 6 =====
  method               circuits   depth  total cx      cos   x PS cx
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  parameter-shift           144      14       720   1.0000      1.00
  QLTO V3 (QPE k=4)           4    1976      3796   0.9672      5.27
  QLTO V4 (direct)           12      21       204   0.9745      0.28
    V4 norm ratio |g|/|gx| = 0.7879   (sinc(R) = 0.9411 is the predicted attenuation)

  The test: does V4 keep circuits << parameter-shift while bringing total
  cx BELOW 1.0x and depth back to a small multiple of the ansatz? If so the
  QPE ladder was a cost with no matching benefit at these G, and V4 is the
  version of this method that can actually run on hardware.
